## Appendix B — sources

Compiled files read at snapshot 8badc05; every figure traces through them to `docs/raw/` (`trace.md`, this folder): `findings/director-brief-2026-09-23.md` (the failed brief); `method/scope.md`, `glossary.md`, `trust-rubric.md`, `plan.md` §Evidence bar; `findings/trigger-timeline.md`, `market-potential.md`, `ai-ads-evidence.md`, `demand-map.md`, `proof-scorecard.md`, `transition-evidence.md`, `whitespace.md` §Risk register, `unknowns.md`; `markets/paid-placement.md`, `organic-recommendation.md`, `agentic-commerce.md`; `competitors/INDEX.md`; `customers/skincare-beauty.md`, `b2b-saas.md`, `high-cpa-regulated.md`, `local-multi-location.md`; `method/blocked-channels.md`.

Strongest single sources: OpenAI run-rate post (`raw/b-openai-1bn-run-rate-milestone-2026-09-22.md`, tier 3); NerdWallet 8-K (`raw/e-case-nerdwallet-earnings-release-2026-02-25-2026-09-22.md`, tier 2); court exhibit ECF 1977-1 (`raw/a-court-mdl-microsoft-ctr-data-2026-09-22.md`, tier 2); Semrush filing (`raw/a-semrush-filing-2026-09-22.md`, tier 2); DSA designation table (`raw/b-eu-dsa-ad-repositories-table-2026-09-22.md`, tier 2); optimisation-lever replication (`raw/e-case-c11-arxiv-tw3-partners-geo-score-2026-09-22.md`, tier 4).

## Glossary

| Term | Meaning here |
|---|---|
| AI; engine | Artificial intelligence; one assistant product (ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Copilot, Claude, Rufus) |
| AI Overviews; AI Mode | Google's AI answer block on a results page; Google's conversational search tab. Both distinct from the Gemini app |
| Copilot; Rufus | Microsoft's assistant; Amazon's shopping assistant |
| GEO; AEO; AI visibility | Generative engine optimisation; answer engine optimisation — names for the organic sub-market. GEO is never geographic here |
| SEO | Search engine optimisation, classical |
| Visibility; traffic; sales | Brand appears in an AI answer; a session referred from an AI surface; revenue attributed to an AI surface |
| Cell | One sub-market × vertical × buyer size. Verticals: skincare and beauty; B2B SaaS (business-to-business software as a service); high-CPA regulated (cost per acquisition: credit cards, insurance, supplements); local and multi-location added separately. Sizes: SMB (small and medium business), mid-market, enterprise |
| spend / attention / none — checked / blank | A cell read: money moved; interest only; every signal run and nothing found; not yet checked |
| Strict / loose | Whether a channel blocked-and-logged counts as checked for a `none` read: no (strict) or yes (loose) |
| Tier | Source provenance 1–7: 1 measured by us; 2 filed (filing, court exhibit); 3 platform's own pages; 4 panel or clickstream; 5 vendor study with n; 6 vendor blog, no n; 7 listicle |
| Source kind | vendor-reported; analyst-derived; filed; company-stated; measured-by-us |
| Gold / Silver / Bronze | Case grades: causal design (holdout, geo-split, switchback); pre/post with an unaffected control; visibility change only |
| raw / rule-1 | Two grade readings: as the screener assigned it; the literal rule that any missing item of the seven-item bar caps a case at Bronze |
| R1 / R2 | Two evidence-class readings: pre/post with control counted as experimental (R1) or observational (R2) |
| Load-bearing claim | A compiled claim a finding rests on; the bar is 80% at tier 3 or better |
| Hypothesis marks | confirmed; killed; unresolved — checked; not produced (producing work did not run); dual = two marks under two readings |
| ARR | Annual recurring revenue |
| MAU | Monthly active users, as each engine defines them |
| Q1 | First calendar quarter |
| CMA | UK Competition and Markets Authority |
| EU AI Act Art. 50 | Article requiring AI-interaction notice and synthetic-content marking; names no assistant |
| VLOSE | Very Large Online Search Engine, a designation under the EU Digital Services Act; an ad-repository duty follows |
| Prompt set | The fixed prompts a vendor's visibility score is run on |
| Own engine sampling | The programme's measured-by-us runs of prompts against engines; one partial day exists, 2026-09-22 |
